+### [Transvoxel](6277-transvoxel.md)
+A level-of-detail (LOD) technique for isosurface extraction that maintains a watertight mesh when neighboring voxels in a hierarchical grid have different resolutions. It solves the gap problem inherent in standard LOD transitions by introducing transition cells that interpolate vertices between coarse and fine grids, ensuring continuity across resolution boundaries. Unlike standard Marching Cubes which assumes uniform voxel size, Transvoxel adapts vertex positions and normals based on the LOD of adjacent voxels.
 
 ### [Dual Contouring and Surface Nets](6319-dual-contouring-and-surface-nets.md)
-Generate a single vertex per active grid cell (voxel) rather than placing vertices on cell edges like Marching Cubes. This family prioritizes mesh sparsity and feature preservation over topological simplicity, producing watertight meshes with fewer triangles. Dual Contouring optimizes vertex position via a Quadratic Error Function (QEF) to preserve sharp features, while Surface Nets uses a weighted average of intersection points for a faster, normal-free approximation.
+Generate a single vertex per active grid cell (voxel) rather than placing vertices on cell edges like Marching Cubes [G]. This family prioritizes mesh sparsity and feature preservation over topological simplicity, producing watertight meshes with fewer triangles [G]. Dual Contouring optimizes vertex position via a Quadratic Error Function (QEF) to preserve sharp features [778-dual-contouring.md], while Surface Nets uses a weighted average of intersection points for a faster, normal-free approximation [921-surface-nets.md].
 
 ### [Neural and Learning-based Extraction](6371-neural-and-learning-based-extraction.md)
-Generates isosurfaces from implicit fields learned by neural networks (e.g., NeRF, DVR, SDF networks) by integrating the extraction process into the optimization loop or using adaptive sampling strategies. Unlike static methods like [Marching Cubes](30-isosurface-extraction.md) or [Surface Nets](921-surface-nets.md) that operate on a fixed grid, these methods allow the mesh topology and geometry to be refined via backpropagation, enabling direct optimization of visual, geometric, or physical objectives. It sets itself apart from siblings by treating the isosurface extraction as a differentiable operation or an adaptive query process, rather than a post-processing step on a discretized volume.
+Extracts triangle meshes from neural implicit representations (occupancy fields, SDFs, or NeRF densities) by combining neural query capabilities with geometric extraction algorithms. It solves the problem of converting continuous, learned volumetric functions into explicit polygonal meshes suitable for rendering or simulation. Unlike static methods like [Marching Cubes](30-isosurface-extraction.md) on fixed grids, this family distinguishes itself by either adaptively querying the neural network to save computation (e.g., MISE) or by making the extraction process fully differentiable to allow gradient-based optimization of the mesh geometry (e.g., FlexiCubes).
 
-#### 2+D Pen-and-Ink for Volume Visualization
-A method where 2D strokes are generated based on 3D information associated with original 3D objects, treating isosurfaces as opaque objects for image buffer generation [S6, unofficial]. It extracts isosurfaces from the raw dataset, treats them as opaque objects for the generation of image buffers (lighting, depth, normals, curvature), and uses these buffers as inputs to pen-and-ink filters to synthesize a final image [S6, unofficial].
+### [Two-Step Surface Reconstruction Method](7364-two-step-surface-reconstruction-method.md)
+Accelerates Marching Cubes by using a lower expansion order FMM evaluation to filter non-boundary voxels, then using a higher expansion order FMM evaluation only on potential boundary voxels to extract the isosurface.
+
+### [Adaptive Minimum Projected Size Adjustment](7457-adaptive-minimum-projected-size-adjustment.md)
+Automatically adjusts the minimum projected size of surface elements frame-to-frame to maintain a target framerate during user interaction, preventing poor or over-populated geometry at varying camera distances.
+
+### [Non-reconnected Multiresolution Isosurfacing](7512-non-reconnected-multiresolution-isosurfacing.md)
+Intentionally omits surface reconnection between adjacent cells of different resolutions to avoid tracking overhead, relying on sufficient polygon density to keep cracks visually negligible.
+
+### [Region-growing Iso-surface Extraction](7568-region-growing-iso-surface-extraction.md)
+A region-growing based iso-surface extraction algorithm that generates high-quality curvature-adaptive semi-regular meshes, preserves sharp features, and extracts all disjoint components of the iso-surface.
+
+### [Generalized Marching Cubes](8320-generalized-marching-cubes.md)
+A contouring method applied to generate triangulated mesh surfaces from the classified volumetric model, capable of dealing with both CT values and material types.
+
+### [Grid Traversal and Data Structure Adaptation](8340-grid-traversal-and-data-structure-adaptation.md)
+Extracts isosurfaces from scalar fields by adapting the underlying spatial data structure to the geometry, rather than iterating over a fixed uniform grid. By using hierarchical structures like octrees or sparse hash maps, these algorithms reduce memory usage and computational cost by only processing cells where the surface exists or varies significantly. They set themselves apart from sibling methods like [Transvoxel](6277-transvoxel.md) by relying on standard topological triangulation rules (e.g., Marching Cubes) applied to adapted domains, often requiring specific traversal logic to handle mismatched refinement levels between adjacent cells.
+
